1
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:04,871
‪PREVIOUSLY ON <i>‪CHOSEN HOME</i>

2
00:00:04,938 --> 00:00:06,072
<i>Gentle-hearted gay man Genichi Hatano</i>

3
00:00:06,139 --> 00:00:07,941
<i>and his partner Saku Sakuta,</i>

4
00:00:08,508 --> 00:00:11,044
<i>end up forming a parent-child contract</i>
<i>with Hotaru Kusunoki.</i>

5
00:00:11,111 --> 00:00:13,880
<i>As Hotaru wants to make guitars</i>
<i>after middle school,</i>

6
00:00:13,947 --> 00:00:15,348
- <i>the three set out for Nagano</i>
- I'll be off now.

7
00:00:15,415 --> 00:00:17,384
<i>for the sake of her dream.</i>

8
00:00:18,685 --> 00:00:20,086
Just a little more to go.

9
00:00:20,153 --> 00:00:20,987
CRAFTSMEN WANTED

10
00:00:25,358 --> 00:00:26,559
Are you okay?

11
00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:28,695
Hello?

12
00:00:34,134 --> 00:00:36,403
Let's take a little break, shall we?

13
00:00:39,172 --> 00:00:40,640
My heart is kind of racing…

14
00:00:41,708 --> 00:00:42,542
Mr. Sakuta.

15
00:00:42,609 --> 00:00:45,111
My hands are shaking
even though it’s not cold.

16
00:00:45,845 --> 00:00:47,614
You’re just nervous.

17
00:00:48,615 --> 00:00:49,449
Want to practice?

18
00:00:49,516 --> 00:00:50,617
Practice what?

19
00:00:51,718 --> 00:00:54,287
I’ll be the person at the guitar workshop.

20
00:00:58,558 --> 00:01:00,160
Hello, welcome.

21
00:01:00,994 --> 00:01:04,664
I’m from Zenpukuji Middle School in Tokyo.

22
00:01:04,731 --> 00:01:06,132
My name is Hotaru Kusunoki.

23
00:01:07,133 --> 00:01:10,003
Why did you want to come
tour our workshop?

24
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:11,104
I…

25
00:01:11,604 --> 00:01:14,607
want to be a guitar maker in the future.

26
00:01:14,674 --> 00:01:16,042
I hope I can.

27
00:01:16,109 --> 00:01:18,478
I read the pamphlet for your guitars

28
00:01:18,545 --> 00:01:22,348
and felt really inspired so I wanted
to come and take a look.

29
00:01:23,383 --> 00:01:24,551
Perfect!

30
00:01:27,153 --> 00:01:28,822
WINNER

31
00:01:28,888 --> 00:01:30,323
Even the gods say you'll be fine.

32
00:01:33,726 --> 00:01:34,494
NO PRIZE

33
00:01:34,561 --> 00:01:35,995
We're a match.

34
00:01:40,567 --> 00:01:44,037
Thanks for having us. I’m Sakuta,
we spoke before regarding the tour.

35
00:01:44,104 --> 00:01:45,905
I’m the head of this workshop.

36
00:01:45,972 --> 00:01:46,973
My name is Yasuo Kishibe.

37
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:49,576
I came from Zenpukuji Middle School.

38
00:01:49,642 --> 00:01:50,777
My name is Hotaru Kusunoki.

39
00:01:51,344 --> 00:01:53,480
This is my homeroom teacher, Mr. Sakuta…

40
00:01:53,546 --> 00:01:55,715
- And I'm her attendant, Hatano.
- I see.

41
00:01:56,349 --> 00:01:58,084
Um, I read your pamphlet,

42
00:01:58,151 --> 00:02:00,553
but I can’t actually play
the guitar at all.

43
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:02,555
Could I still learn to make them?

44
00:02:02,622 --> 00:02:03,590
Could I work here?

45
00:02:03,656 --> 00:02:06,493
We’d really appreciate any guidance
you could give this child.

46
00:02:07,127 --> 00:02:08,661
Calm down, the both of you.

47
00:02:09,662 --> 00:02:11,164
In any case,

48
00:02:11,231 --> 00:02:12,866
why don’t we go take a look inside?

49
00:02:12,932 --> 00:02:13,800
Okay.

50
00:02:16,636 --> 00:02:18,938
TOBISHIMA

51
00:02:19,606 --> 00:02:22,075
Do all of these become guitars?

52
00:02:22,142 --> 00:02:23,309
That's right.

53
00:02:23,376 --> 00:02:26,212
Even the ones with knots like this.

54
00:02:26,279 --> 00:02:27,780
Really?

55
00:02:28,314 --> 00:02:31,718
We think things like that
give it character.

56
00:02:32,218 --> 00:02:34,621
If they all looked the same,
it’d be boring, no?

57
00:02:34,687 --> 00:02:35,588
True.

58
00:02:36,122 --> 00:02:39,826
Do you know how a guitar makes sound?

59
00:02:39,893 --> 00:02:41,594
The strings get plucked…?

60
00:02:41,661 --> 00:02:43,997
The vibration then travels
to the top plate…

61
00:02:44,063 --> 00:02:46,432
And the air inside vibrates too.

62
00:02:46,499 --> 00:02:47,333
Exactly.

63
00:02:47,834 --> 00:02:49,903
All of it works together.

64
00:02:49,969 --> 00:02:51,704
So every part matters.

65
00:02:52,338 --> 00:02:54,741
We do adjustments depending on the wood,
taking it slow,

66
00:02:54,807 --> 00:02:58,144
and that’s how you shape it
into a clean guitar body.

67
00:02:58,211 --> 00:03:00,380
Rush it or force it,

68
00:03:00,446 --> 00:03:01,414
and it’ll crack.

69
00:03:02,549 --> 00:03:04,250
That step affects things such as the tone

70
00:03:04,317 --> 00:03:06,853
and strength of a guitar.
It’s a crucial step.

71
00:03:07,453 --> 00:03:10,590
For us, good sound is a given.

72
00:03:10,657 --> 00:03:12,559
But we also make guitars
that last a long time

73
00:03:12,625 --> 00:03:14,594
and grow with the person who plays them.

74
00:03:15,361 --> 00:03:17,530
Those are the kind of guitars
we're aiming for.

75
00:03:17,597 --> 00:03:19,666
Do guitars grow?

76
00:03:20,166 --> 00:03:21,668
Even with the same guitar,

77
00:03:21,734 --> 00:03:24,437
the sound changes
depending on how you play it.

78
00:03:24,504 --> 00:03:26,806
It becomes a tone
only that person can make.

79
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:30,109
I wonder if that’s true
for Mr. Hatano's guitar too.

80
00:03:30,643 --> 00:03:31,611
It has a good sound?

81
00:03:33,112 --> 00:03:34,847
It's a sound that I like.

82
00:03:35,615 --> 00:03:36,549
I see now.

83
00:03:37,050 --> 00:03:39,052
So that’s why you want to make guitars.

84
00:03:41,454 --> 00:03:42,956
Any thoughts after the tour?

85
00:03:43,690 --> 00:03:44,991
I want to work here.

86
00:03:45,058 --> 00:03:46,893
I don’t know if I'm up for the task,

87
00:03:46,960 --> 00:03:48,995
but I want to learn to make guitars too.

88
00:03:49,796 --> 00:03:51,464
And after listening to you,

89
00:03:51,531 --> 00:03:53,333
the things you value here

90
00:03:53,399 --> 00:03:55,802
is something I'd like to value as well.

91
00:03:56,669 --> 00:03:58,338
Thank you. But…

92
00:03:58,972 --> 00:04:01,374
You won’t be making guitars right away.

93
00:04:01,441 --> 00:04:04,644
First you learn the structure.

94
00:04:05,345 --> 00:04:06,946
Then how to read and make blueprints,

95
00:04:07,547 --> 00:04:09,048
study design,

96
00:04:09,115 --> 00:04:11,517
learn the tools and practice…

97
00:04:11,584 --> 00:04:14,654
Before you can make anything decent,

98
00:04:15,154 --> 00:04:16,589
it’ll take at least ten years.

99
00:04:18,958 --> 00:04:20,593
More so than you expect, Ms. Kusunoki,

100
00:04:21,094 --> 00:04:23,796
I think you'll probably face
many challenges.

101
00:04:24,530 --> 00:04:27,133
Even so, do you still want to work here?

102
00:04:27,934 --> 00:04:30,236
- Take your time and think--
- I want to work here!

103
00:04:30,870 --> 00:04:33,273
- What?
- I want to work here!

104
00:04:33,339 --> 00:04:34,707
Please!

105
00:04:36,943 --> 00:04:39,879
Um, I think Hotaru is a resilient kid.

106
00:04:40,513 --> 00:04:43,549
I agree too, as her homeroom teacher.

107
00:04:43,616 --> 00:04:46,119
To be specific about Hotaru’s good points,

108
00:04:46,185 --> 00:04:48,988
first, she has good table manners.

109
00:04:49,489 --> 00:04:50,556
Also,

110
00:04:50,623 --> 00:04:53,459
she’s really good
at gently petting animals.

111
00:04:54,060 --> 00:04:55,094
And, uh,

112
00:04:55,161 --> 00:04:57,664
- the first time she played the gui--
- That's enough!

113
00:04:57,730 --> 00:04:58,564
Sorry.

114
00:05:00,933 --> 00:05:02,001
Very well.

115
00:05:02,969 --> 00:05:05,071
Those who have a sound they love…

116
00:05:05,838 --> 00:05:07,640
are those who can push through.

117
00:05:08,675 --> 00:05:09,776
It's our pleasure

118
00:05:09,842 --> 00:05:11,311
to have you with us!

119
00:05:12,945 --> 00:05:14,514
Thank you!

120
00:05:17,517 --> 00:05:20,586
You said you wanted to see
the finished guitars too, right?

121
00:05:20,653 --> 00:05:21,587
Yes.

122
00:05:21,654 --> 00:05:23,489
Hey, Kazuki!

123
00:05:24,090 --> 00:05:24,957
Come here for a bit.

124
00:05:25,825 --> 00:05:27,126
This is my grandson.

125
00:05:27,694 --> 00:05:29,195
He helps out sometimes.

126
00:05:30,797 --> 00:05:32,932
Show them the exhibition room, would you?

127
00:05:32,999 --> 00:05:34,667
Okay. This way, please.

128
00:05:35,568 --> 00:05:37,036
- Thank you.
- Um!

129
00:05:37,937 --> 00:05:40,440
I have one more thing to ask you.

130
00:05:42,275 --> 00:05:45,445
All the guitars we make
mostly end up displayed here.

131
00:05:46,479 --> 00:05:48,614
Feel free to get a feel or play them.

132
00:05:50,616 --> 00:05:51,784
I can’t play.

133
00:05:52,652 --> 00:05:53,853
Sorry.

134
00:05:55,088 --> 00:05:57,390
Playing and making are totally different.

135
00:05:57,890 --> 00:05:59,292
It's fine even if you can't play.

136
00:05:59,859 --> 00:06:01,260
Thank you.

137
00:06:04,297 --> 00:06:05,331
Actually, that’s a lie.

138
00:06:06,299 --> 00:06:08,301
Everyone here can play,

139
00:06:08,835 --> 00:06:10,503
so it might help to know a bit.

140
00:06:11,170 --> 00:06:12,004
Huh?

141
00:06:12,638 --> 00:06:15,808
If you’re different from everyone else,
doesn’t it feel awkward?

142
00:06:17,210 --> 00:06:19,912
Do you ever feel awkward?

143
00:06:22,949 --> 00:06:24,517
This is cute!

144
00:06:26,018 --> 00:06:28,454
Excuse me. Can I get three of these?

145
00:06:28,521 --> 00:06:29,922
Thank you.

146
00:06:30,423 --> 00:06:32,692
That'll be 12,000 yen.

147
00:06:33,526 --> 00:06:34,761
Here you go.

148
00:06:34,827 --> 00:06:36,529
That's the exact amount.

149
00:06:36,596 --> 00:06:37,597
Why three?

150
00:06:38,398 --> 00:06:39,532
What are you doing?

151
00:06:39,599 --> 00:06:41,434
For you. Here you go.

152
00:06:41,934 --> 00:06:43,069
You too.

153
00:06:43,836 --> 00:06:44,704
Now we all match.

154
00:06:45,505 --> 00:06:47,473
You’re very close, aren’t you?
That’s good.

155
00:06:49,108 --> 00:06:51,210
Okay then. We’ll be waiting for you.

156
00:06:52,044 --> 00:06:53,012
Thank you.

157
00:07:00,520 --> 00:07:01,788
- Thanks for your help.
- Yeah.

158
00:07:03,723 --> 00:07:06,125
Kazuki! Hey, Kazuki!

159
00:07:06,626 --> 00:07:08,261
- Mind if we ask something?
- Yeah?

160
00:07:08,327 --> 00:07:09,929
Who was that girl earlier?

161
00:07:09,996 --> 00:07:11,364
She came to tour the workshop.

162
00:07:11,864 --> 00:07:14,634
- Love is finally in the air for you!
- It's nothing like that.

163
00:07:14,700 --> 00:07:16,702
But is she your type though?

164
00:07:19,305 --> 00:07:20,440
Well, I guess so.

165
00:07:20,506 --> 00:07:22,074
That’s the first time Kazuki said that!

166
00:07:22,141 --> 00:07:23,443
We'll be cheering for you!

167
00:07:23,509 --> 00:07:24,343
Isn't that right?

168
00:07:31,984 --> 00:07:33,853
I’ll work really hard.

169
00:07:34,420 --> 00:07:36,689
It might take a long time,

170
00:07:36,756 --> 00:07:38,491
but I want to be able to make guitars.

171
00:07:39,192 --> 00:07:41,327
And when I do, Mr. Hatano, please play it.

172
00:07:41,394 --> 00:07:42,228
Sure.

173
00:07:42,295 --> 00:07:45,164
Mr. Sakuta can then listen.

174
00:07:45,231 --> 00:07:47,533
We'll have to live a long life then, huh.

175
00:07:50,903 --> 00:07:52,538
Take a look at this, Hotaru.

176
00:07:53,206 --> 00:07:55,942
- Here.
- There’s a high school near the workshop.

177
00:07:56,008 --> 00:07:58,377
It has a night program too.

178
00:07:58,444 --> 00:08:00,480
I spoke with Mr. Kishibe

179
00:08:00,546 --> 00:08:03,382
and he said it’d be fine
to work while schooling.

180
00:08:03,883 --> 00:08:07,386
His grandson Kazuki
is in the regular course there too.

181
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:09,722
Work and school,

182
00:08:09,789 --> 00:08:12,358
Sakuta really wants you to go for both--

183
00:08:12,425 --> 00:08:14,594
- Hey!
- Sorry.

184
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:16,896
You get to decide, of course.

185
00:08:17,597 --> 00:08:19,265
Just know that option exists.

186
00:08:19,866 --> 00:08:20,766
Thank you.

187
00:08:21,367 --> 00:08:22,401
Don't mention it.

188
00:08:23,035 --> 00:08:26,072
U-Um, can we make a quick detour?

189
00:08:26,672 --> 00:08:29,675
NAGANO SOUVENIR

190
00:08:33,613 --> 00:08:34,547
Wait, isn't this?

191
00:08:34,614 --> 00:08:37,416
I found it while sorting through
the apartment listings this morning,

192
00:08:37,483 --> 00:08:38,518
and I kept it in my pocket.

193
00:08:39,151 --> 00:08:40,186
Hey, wait!

194
00:08:40,887 --> 00:08:41,754
What's the matter?

195
00:08:41,821 --> 00:08:43,422
I should be asking you that.

196
00:08:43,489 --> 00:08:44,323
Are you okay with it?

197
00:08:45,124 --> 00:08:47,894
I’m throwing it away
properly myself this time.

198
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:49,295
Yeah, but

199
00:08:49,362 --> 00:08:52,131
you should part
with important things properly.

200
00:08:52,198 --> 00:08:53,766
What do you mean by that?

201
00:08:54,333 --> 00:08:55,301
Well…

202
00:08:58,004 --> 00:08:59,038
NAGANO PREFECTURE

203
00:08:59,105 --> 00:09:00,106
I found it.

204
00:09:08,848 --> 00:09:09,849
Coming.

205
00:09:12,552 --> 00:09:13,386
Are things okay?

206
00:09:14,120 --> 00:09:16,689
Once I’m done getting ready,
I’ll go to the police.

207
00:09:16,756 --> 00:09:19,125
Before that, I called Ms. Matsu.

208
00:09:19,825 --> 00:09:20,893
Who's that?

209
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:23,195
She's the officer I mentioned before.

210
00:09:23,696 --> 00:09:24,764
You can trust her.

211
00:09:25,331 --> 00:09:26,599
She'll look out for you, Tomoe.

212
00:09:26,666 --> 00:09:28,701
I believe Ms. Matsu
will take this seriously.

213
00:09:29,268 --> 00:09:30,102
I see.

214
00:09:31,437 --> 00:09:33,439
Speaking of the devil,

215
00:09:33,506 --> 00:09:34,473
she's here.

216
00:09:36,042 --> 00:09:39,545
I understand the circumstances of the
embezzlement and your reason for fleeing.

217
00:09:40,413 --> 00:09:43,215
To ensure you’re not treated unfairly,

218
00:09:43,282 --> 00:09:46,752
I’ll explain clearly
to the investigating officer.

219
00:09:46,819 --> 00:09:48,754
So when you give
your statement at the station,

220
00:09:48,821 --> 00:09:50,289
please be honest.

221
00:09:50,356 --> 00:09:51,324
I understand.

222
00:09:52,091 --> 00:09:55,127
The 32,261,570 yen that you took

223
00:09:55,194 --> 00:09:57,897
is all in there?

224
00:09:57,964 --> 00:09:58,798
Yes.

225
00:09:58,864 --> 00:10:01,334
Were all your belongings stolen
during your escape?

226
00:10:02,201 --> 00:10:05,037
But my wallet was in my pocket.

227
00:10:05,104 --> 00:10:07,173
Then you should bring that with you too.

228
00:10:07,239 --> 00:10:08,874
Okay.

229
00:10:14,013 --> 00:10:15,848
Don’t throw any of those away.

230
00:10:15,915 --> 00:10:17,717
I'm just organizing them.

231
00:10:17,783 --> 00:10:19,352
By date, at least.

232
00:10:20,686 --> 00:10:23,422
You’re quite the meticulous fugitive.

233
00:10:23,923 --> 00:10:26,592
It's an old habit from accounting work
that I still have with me.

234
00:10:26,659 --> 00:10:27,560
RECEIPTS

235
00:10:27,627 --> 00:10:30,162
Most of these are receipts
for keychains, huh?

236
00:10:30,830 --> 00:10:32,431
Wait, what about this one?

237
00:10:33,232 --> 00:10:36,535
Stomach medicine at a pharmacy in Kagawa?

238
00:10:36,602 --> 00:10:38,604
I thought I’d save money

239
00:10:38,671 --> 00:10:40,706
and I tried eating some plants
by the roadside,

240
00:10:40,773 --> 00:10:42,174
but it gave me a stomachache.

241
00:10:42,241 --> 00:10:43,609
You’re wild.

242
00:10:44,710 --> 00:10:47,113
This one is from a supermarket in Iwate,

243
00:10:47,179 --> 00:10:48,314
and you purchased soy sauce.

244
00:10:48,381 --> 00:10:50,716
I went fishing
with some folks at the port,

245
00:10:50,783 --> 00:10:52,251
and they gave me <i>sashimi.</i>

246
00:10:52,985 --> 00:10:56,455
Kumamoto, Fukushima…

247
00:10:56,522 --> 00:10:57,957
And Okinawa too.

248
00:10:58,024 --> 00:11:01,060
You’ve been to a lot of places.

249
00:11:01,127 --> 00:11:02,862
If I wanted to go somewhere,

250
00:11:02,928 --> 00:11:04,830
I could just go.

251
00:11:05,398 --> 00:11:06,432
Really?

252
00:11:06,499 --> 00:11:09,735
I used to think it was impossible,
but surprisingly it wasn't.

253
00:11:10,903 --> 00:11:13,606
Then maybe I could go anywhere too?

254
00:11:13,673 --> 00:11:14,507
What?

255
00:11:14,573 --> 00:11:15,975
I've…

256
00:11:16,042 --> 00:11:19,078
been here for so long.

257
00:11:19,812 --> 00:11:21,814
So I can’t really imagine myself

258
00:11:21,881 --> 00:11:23,849
being anywhere else.

259
00:11:25,084 --> 00:11:26,986
But after seeing this, you know?

260
00:11:27,653 --> 00:11:28,954
Maybe I can.

261
00:11:31,691 --> 00:11:33,726
Sorry, Ms. Matsu.

262
00:11:33,793 --> 00:11:37,496
I told one little lie earlier.

263
00:11:38,164 --> 00:11:39,265
What?

264
00:11:41,300 --> 00:11:42,368
- Ah!
- Oh dear!

265
00:11:45,638 --> 00:11:46,772
Is something wrong?

266
00:11:48,607 --> 00:11:51,043
Can I lie about my job here?

267
00:11:51,110 --> 00:11:53,379
What are you saying?
Of course you can’t do that.

268
00:11:53,446 --> 00:11:56,716
Then what should I write
if I'm a day laborer?

269
00:11:56,782 --> 00:11:57,883
Oh.

270
00:11:58,951 --> 00:12:00,219
In that case,

271
00:12:00,286 --> 00:12:02,988
it might be tough to find a place.

272
00:12:03,823 --> 00:12:04,790
Are you serious?

273
00:12:04,857 --> 00:12:06,225
Then, find me a job!

274
00:12:06,792 --> 00:12:08,861
Even if you say that…

275
00:12:08,928 --> 00:12:09,995
This guy

276
00:12:10,062 --> 00:12:12,198
has been eating less than before.

277
00:12:12,765 --> 00:12:14,133
I researched and…

278
00:12:14,734 --> 00:12:15,801
it might be stress.

279
00:12:16,602 --> 00:12:19,872
He’s sensitive, so a safe room
with the right temperature

280
00:12:19,939 --> 00:12:21,741
and cleanliness is really important.

281
00:12:22,408 --> 00:12:23,342
That's why!

282
00:12:23,409 --> 00:12:25,377
I gave up on a lot of things for myself,

283
00:12:25,878 --> 00:12:27,213
but for this little guy,

284
00:12:27,980 --> 00:12:29,081
the house…

285
00:12:29,582 --> 00:12:31,584
is something I just can't compromise on!

286
00:12:31,650 --> 00:12:32,818
That's what I thought.

287
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:37,323
Perfect. That’s good. One more time.

288
00:12:37,389 --> 00:12:38,457
Huh? What?

289
00:12:38,524 --> 00:12:40,059
Actually, I started this…

290
00:12:40,726 --> 00:12:42,595
"House-Hunting Struggles: Real Stories."

291
00:12:42,661 --> 00:12:46,132
Most interviews of this kind
show only successful people, right?

292
00:12:46,198 --> 00:12:49,001
So I thought I’d interview people
who are still unsure.

293
00:12:49,068 --> 00:12:51,337
Would that even be helpful?

294
00:12:51,403 --> 00:12:54,640
I think it could definitely
help someone out there.

295
00:12:58,144 --> 00:12:59,779
"It can help someone," he says.

296
00:13:00,379 --> 00:13:02,515
Want to join me for the interview then?

297
00:13:02,581 --> 00:13:05,384
"House-Hunting Struggles: Real Stories
brought to you by Okabe."

298
00:13:05,451 --> 00:13:06,619
Sure.

299
00:13:06,685 --> 00:13:07,653
Good to hear.

300
00:13:08,220 --> 00:13:11,290
It's about a gay couple
looking for a home, right?

301
00:13:11,357 --> 00:13:12,558
That's right.

302
00:13:12,625 --> 00:13:15,961
And about the photos, are you okay
if it’s just from the neck down?

303
00:13:16,695 --> 00:13:18,764
If they're going with that, I don't mind.

304
00:13:19,431 --> 00:13:21,967
Then why don’t we wear this at that time?

305
00:13:22,034 --> 00:13:24,403
Like a couple look.
Even if our faces aren’t shown,

306
00:13:24,470 --> 00:13:25,871
we can show our lovey-dovey vibe.

307
00:13:25,938 --> 00:13:28,741
Hell no! Never!

308
00:13:28,808 --> 00:13:29,708
What?

309
00:13:30,743 --> 00:13:32,444
Please leave it there.

310
00:13:32,945 --> 00:13:33,813
Sorry about this.

311
00:13:37,416 --> 00:13:40,352
So what was the lie?

312
00:13:42,588 --> 00:13:43,989
That…

313
00:13:45,658 --> 00:13:47,359
I embezzled because

314
00:13:47,426 --> 00:13:49,028
I wanted to be a mom who didn’t

315
00:13:49,094 --> 00:13:50,796
want her child to worry about money.

316
00:13:51,363 --> 00:13:52,631
And that I ran away

317
00:13:53,365 --> 00:13:55,267
to chase my dreams.

318
00:13:55,334 --> 00:13:56,936
Those were lies?

319
00:13:58,404 --> 00:14:00,506
While talking earlier, I realized…

320
00:14:02,274 --> 00:14:03,776
Thinking about myself,

321
00:14:04,743 --> 00:14:07,746
and going wherever I wanted each day…

322
00:14:08,514 --> 00:14:10,015
It was fun.

323
00:14:11,851 --> 00:14:13,185
But in the end…

324
00:14:13,686 --> 00:14:16,589
maybe I just wanted to quit.

325
00:14:17,089 --> 00:14:18,591
Quit being a mom,

326
00:14:18,657 --> 00:14:20,459
quit being an accounting temp…

327
00:14:21,026 --> 00:14:22,528
I just wanted to wreck it all

328
00:14:23,128 --> 00:14:25,097
and walk away from all of it.

329
00:14:29,368 --> 00:14:30,636
I’m sorry.

330
00:14:31,237 --> 00:14:33,072
I really am the worst.

331
00:14:33,138 --> 00:14:34,607
You are.

332
00:14:35,107 --> 00:14:36,408
Yes.

333
00:14:37,309 --> 00:14:39,745
But I kind of understand you, Mrs. Tomoe.

334
00:14:39,812 --> 00:14:41,046
Sometimes at work,

335
00:14:41,113 --> 00:14:42,548
I wish a bomb would fall

336
00:14:42,615 --> 00:14:44,550
so I could have the day off.

337
00:14:44,617 --> 00:14:46,518
You think about that, Ms. Matsu?

338
00:14:46,585 --> 00:14:48,354
- Sometimes.
- Oh!

339
00:14:48,420 --> 00:14:49,822
Like, when you see the trees

340
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:51,824
or flowers you really love in the garden,

341
00:14:51,891 --> 00:14:56,028
but today
watering them feels like a chore…

342
00:14:56,095 --> 00:14:57,563
Your feelings are like that, yes?

343
00:14:57,630 --> 00:14:58,497
Exactly!

344
00:15:00,132 --> 00:15:01,166
Seems like a no.

345
00:15:01,667 --> 00:15:05,804
Uh, thank you. You can stop there.

346
00:15:09,508 --> 00:15:10,643
Maybe…

347
00:15:11,143 --> 00:15:13,545
I should've said all this sooner.

348
00:15:14,947 --> 00:15:17,049
I should've meddled more too.

349
00:15:17,116 --> 00:15:19,551
Maybe then I could’ve told you

350
00:15:19,618 --> 00:15:21,320
"you’re the worst" sooner.

351
00:15:21,387 --> 00:15:23,322
I was the one who is at fault.

352
00:15:23,389 --> 00:15:24,757
No need to blame yourself.

353
00:15:25,591 --> 00:15:26,592
That’s not true.

354
00:15:27,159 --> 00:15:28,394
Not at all.

355
00:15:30,462 --> 00:15:34,066
I know I probably can’t undo
what’s been done.

356
00:15:34,867 --> 00:15:35,935
But still…

357
00:15:36,602 --> 00:15:37,770
the things I've broken,

358
00:15:38,504 --> 00:15:41,473
I want to fix them one at a time.

359
00:15:59,124 --> 00:15:59,959
INOKASHIRA APARTMENTS

360
00:16:00,025 --> 00:16:01,527
Thank you for driving us back.

361
00:16:01,593 --> 00:16:03,095
Thank you.

362
00:16:03,595 --> 00:16:04,730
Don't mention it.

363
00:16:08,968 --> 00:16:09,868
Is something wrong?

364
00:16:11,804 --> 00:16:12,871
Has Mom…

365
00:16:13,439 --> 00:16:15,074
already left?

366
00:16:27,853 --> 00:16:30,356
WELCOME BACK

367
00:16:32,224 --> 00:16:33,225
I'm back.

368
00:16:42,234 --> 00:16:43,702
Thank you for the food.

369
00:16:45,204 --> 00:16:47,806
1. APPLICATION PERIOD
2. DATES FOR ACADEMIC EXAMINATIONS

370
00:16:49,775 --> 00:16:53,045
ENTRANCE EXAM

371
00:16:53,112 --> 00:16:54,213
Next.

372
00:16:54,279 --> 00:16:56,949
"Agree with" means to have
the same opinion of something.

373
00:16:57,016 --> 00:16:57,850
That's correct.

374
00:16:59,051 --> 00:17:01,053
You can do it! I know you can!

375
00:17:01,553 --> 00:17:03,188
Hotaru!

376
00:17:03,255 --> 00:17:04,390
Thanks.

377
00:17:04,456 --> 00:17:06,325
But Nagano, huh?

378
00:17:06,392 --> 00:17:07,426
Where’s that again?

379
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:11,230
- Here.
- Oh, it's near then.

380
00:17:11,730 --> 00:17:14,867
Oh, you got a notification
saying something about yearbook.

381
00:17:16,101 --> 00:17:18,170
"For the collage page in the yearbook,

382
00:17:18,237 --> 00:17:21,273
please submit a photo of you."

383
00:17:21,340 --> 00:17:24,176
But I don’t have any photos anyway,
so I’ll just ignore it.

384
00:17:24,243 --> 00:17:26,512
What? Want me to take one for you then?

385
00:17:26,578 --> 00:17:27,780
With us in it?

386
00:17:27,846 --> 00:17:28,680
Oh!

387
00:17:29,815 --> 00:17:31,083
That's a nice idea.

388
00:17:32,484 --> 00:17:34,386
- Nice hoodies.
- Right?

389
00:17:34,453 --> 00:17:36,355
This guy is persistent.

390
00:17:36,422 --> 00:17:37,556
Totally against my will.

391
00:17:40,292 --> 00:17:42,494
- I'm back.
- Welcome back.

392
00:17:43,996 --> 00:17:46,565
What the hell. It’s you two, huh?

393
00:17:46,632 --> 00:17:47,866
That’s our line!

394
00:17:47,933 --> 00:17:49,768
He works for us

395
00:17:49,835 --> 00:17:50,903
as a driver now.

396
00:17:51,737 --> 00:17:54,440
He takes clients to viewings and all that,

397
00:17:54,940 --> 00:17:56,075
and he’s pretty well-liked.

398
00:17:57,042 --> 00:17:59,411
You look kind of nice now.

399
00:17:59,478 --> 00:18:00,879
Your hair, your clothes, etc.

400
00:18:00,946 --> 00:18:02,448
I started taking care of my looks.

401
00:18:03,015 --> 00:18:04,817
To take proper care of a rabbit,

402
00:18:04,883 --> 00:18:06,819
I also have to look after myself.

403
00:18:07,453 --> 00:18:08,954
Is that how it works?

404
00:18:09,021 --> 00:18:11,457
I'll be taking a break
before my next task.

405
00:18:11,523 --> 00:18:12,558
Noted.

406
00:18:14,426 --> 00:18:15,928
I'm back.

407
00:18:15,994 --> 00:18:16,929
Such a cutie.

408
00:18:16,995 --> 00:18:17,830
HOUSE-HUNTING STRUGGLES: REAL STORIES

409
00:18:17,896 --> 00:18:20,132
Why did you decide to buy a house
in the first place?

410
00:18:20,199 --> 00:18:21,533
Well…

411
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:23,735
Because you saw
the marriage registration form, yes?

412
00:18:24,603 --> 00:18:25,771
What?

413
00:18:26,705 --> 00:18:29,374
The marriage registration form
I’d filled out with my ex,

414
00:18:29,441 --> 00:18:31,343
Hatano saw it by chance.

415
00:18:31,410 --> 00:18:33,979
Just when I was saying things like,

416
00:18:34,046 --> 00:18:36,248
"It doesn’t matter
since we can’t file it,"

417
00:18:36,315 --> 00:18:37,916
Hatano said, "Instead of marriage,

418
00:18:37,983 --> 00:18:40,586
how about buying a house as a 'clamp'?"

419
00:18:40,652 --> 00:18:42,588
I see how it is now.

420
00:18:43,288 --> 00:18:44,723
You guys…

421
00:18:44,790 --> 00:18:47,126
Why are you so hung up
on getting married anyway?

422
00:18:47,192 --> 00:18:48,026
What?

423
00:18:48,093 --> 00:18:50,195
Getting married
doesn’t guarantee happiness.

424
00:18:51,396 --> 00:18:54,233
I also don’t believe that marriage

425
00:18:54,733 --> 00:18:56,435
is something absolute

426
00:18:56,502 --> 00:18:58,937
or a symbol of happiness.

427
00:18:59,571 --> 00:19:01,907
I just want to be recognized.

428
00:19:02,674 --> 00:19:04,143
Just like everybody else,

429
00:19:04,209 --> 00:19:07,412
whether to get married or not,
I want to be able to choose.

430
00:19:07,980 --> 00:19:10,048
That would mean

431
00:19:10,115 --> 00:19:12,317
we’re allowed to be who we are.

432
00:19:12,384 --> 00:19:13,852
That's how I see it.

433
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:16,855
I don't get it.

434
00:19:16,922 --> 00:19:17,990
Mr. Ichigaya.

435
00:19:18,490 --> 00:19:19,958
Remind me again

436
00:19:20,025 --> 00:19:21,493
why you two can’t get married.

437
00:19:22,094 --> 00:19:24,496
- Who cares, right?
- Huh?

438
00:19:24,563 --> 00:19:26,231
If you can’t get married,

439
00:19:26,732 --> 00:19:28,333
then just make it so you can.

440
00:19:29,168 --> 00:19:30,035
Start a revolution.

441
00:19:31,103 --> 00:19:32,571
"Love and revolution", yes?

442
00:19:34,106 --> 00:19:37,042
- You're right!
- You’re making fun of us, aren’t you?

443
00:19:37,109 --> 00:19:39,511
Not my problem anyway.
Anyway, I’m heading out.

444
00:19:40,312 --> 00:19:42,047
- See you.
- Goodbye.

445
00:19:42,114 --> 00:19:43,015
Bye.

446
00:19:49,922 --> 00:19:51,924
Over here! Hurry.

447
00:19:51,990 --> 00:19:54,159
THIS IS THE REAR GATE. PLEASE USE
MAIN ENTRANCE. NO UNAUTHORIZED VEHICLES

448
00:19:54,226 --> 00:19:56,662
Are you sure you’re okay
with us being in the yearbook?

449
00:19:56,728 --> 00:19:58,764
Hey, you think we can fool them with this?

450
00:19:58,830 --> 00:20:01,033
- I don't know.
- Hey, look!

451
00:20:02,100 --> 00:20:04,336
Don't I look good in this?

452
00:20:04,403 --> 00:20:05,837
<i>During break,</i>

453
00:20:05,904 --> 00:20:08,106
<i>I've always wanted to hang out</i>
<i>at someone’s desk and talk.</i>

454
00:20:08,674 --> 00:20:09,608
<i>I've…</i>

455
00:20:09,675 --> 00:20:11,610
<i>always wanted to borrow the textbook</i>

456
00:20:11,677 --> 00:20:13,612
<i>from the person sitting next to me.</i>

457
00:20:13,679 --> 00:20:16,081
I've always wanted to do
a full-on sprint down the hallway!

458
00:20:18,784 --> 00:20:20,118
- Huh?
- …Until

459
00:20:20,185 --> 00:20:23,322
a teacher yells at me!

460
00:20:23,388 --> 00:20:24,223
Hey!

461
00:20:24,289 --> 00:20:26,124
Look at him.

462
00:20:27,459 --> 00:20:29,161
It looks like we're wearing uniforms.

463
00:20:29,228 --> 00:20:31,129
- Ah!
- What?

464
00:20:31,630 --> 00:20:34,266
What about you, Nacchi?
Anything you wanted to do at school?

465
00:20:35,367 --> 00:20:37,302
Maybe go on a school trip.

466
00:20:37,970 --> 00:20:41,406
A school trip is kinda tough, huh?

467
00:20:42,841 --> 00:20:44,977
Then we’ll save that for next time.

468
00:20:45,477 --> 00:20:46,445
What do you mean?

469
00:20:46,979 --> 00:20:48,480
Next time, let's do it.

470
00:20:49,047 --> 00:20:49,982
It's a promise!

471
00:20:51,516 --> 00:20:52,584
Promise!

472
00:20:56,622 --> 00:20:57,456
Seriously?

473
00:20:57,522 --> 00:20:58,724
You mean it?

474
00:21:07,766 --> 00:21:08,700
GAY

475
00:21:09,268 --> 00:21:10,502
Kazuki!

476
00:21:10,569 --> 00:21:12,237
Yeah?

477
00:21:12,304 --> 00:21:14,473
Could you please show me your math notes?

478
00:21:14,539 --> 00:21:15,440
What?

479
00:21:16,174 --> 00:21:18,443
I slept like a log in class.

480
00:21:18,510 --> 00:21:19,811
There’s a quiz tomorrow, right?

481
00:21:20,779 --> 00:21:21,847
Please!

482
00:21:23,282 --> 00:21:24,783
Only if you buy me juice.

483
00:21:24,850 --> 00:21:26,618
Really? I'll totally do that!

484
00:21:27,119 --> 00:21:28,587
Thanks!

485
00:21:28,654 --> 00:21:30,922
You're gonna be called gay if you do that.

486
00:21:30,989 --> 00:21:32,691
- I'll go get my notes from class.
- Okay.

487
00:21:32,758 --> 00:21:33,925
Gross!

488
00:21:34,693 --> 00:21:35,961
Gross…

489
00:21:36,028 --> 00:21:38,030
So gross, damn it!

490
00:21:39,698 --> 00:21:41,733
I'm really so disgusting!

491
00:21:44,202 --> 00:21:46,204
How many <i>shishamo</i> will you eat?

492
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:50,042
Three? Got it.

493
00:21:51,677 --> 00:21:53,278
The fire seems a little low.

494
00:21:54,046 --> 00:21:55,380
If that's the case,

495
00:21:55,447 --> 00:21:57,683
just add some scrap paper.

496
00:22:00,285 --> 00:22:01,920
It was still in my pocket.

497
00:22:01,987 --> 00:22:03,388
If you want, use this.

498
00:22:03,455 --> 00:22:06,124
No, that’s too important…

499
00:22:06,725 --> 00:22:09,528
Grilling Hotaru’s <i>shishamo</i> properly
is important too.

500
00:22:10,228 --> 00:22:12,197
You're right.

501
00:22:12,964 --> 00:22:14,132
That's why…

502
00:22:15,500 --> 00:22:16,401
There.

503
00:22:21,673 --> 00:22:22,574
It's grilling well.

504
00:22:27,379 --> 00:22:28,413
Hatano.

505
00:22:29,414 --> 00:22:30,415
A marriage registration form…

506
00:22:31,450 --> 00:22:33,118
Want to fill it out with me?

507
00:22:33,185 --> 00:22:34,786
What? Of course.

508
00:22:35,287 --> 00:22:36,288
Let's do it.

509
00:22:37,155 --> 00:22:40,459
After that, let's go file it.

510
00:22:42,461 --> 00:22:43,362
Huh?

511
00:22:44,963 --> 00:22:47,866
To the ward office.
Our marriage registration form.

512
00:22:48,567 --> 00:22:49,668
Let’s go file it.

513
00:22:53,638 --> 00:22:54,473
Okay.

514
00:22:57,476 --> 00:22:59,111
Congratulations!

515
00:22:59,177 --> 00:23:00,379
- Congratulations.
- So cute!

516
00:23:00,445 --> 00:23:02,314
What are you guys celebrating for?

517
00:23:02,381 --> 00:23:03,215
Haven’t you seen?

518
00:23:03,281 --> 00:23:05,650
The results of
the animal illustration contest.

519
00:23:05,717 --> 00:23:06,551
It's already out.

520
00:23:06,618 --> 00:23:10,288
ANIMAL ILLUSTRATION CONTEST RESULTS

521
00:23:12,357 --> 00:23:13,759
- Hello.
- Hello.

522
00:23:13,825 --> 00:23:16,161
You entered the contest too, Ms. Momose?

523
00:23:16,228 --> 00:23:18,096
I did the modelling.

524
00:23:18,163 --> 00:23:20,465
The Toyoko kids drew me.

525
00:23:20,532 --> 00:23:22,200
What, Toyoko?

526
00:23:22,701 --> 00:23:23,769
Is this you, Ms. Momose?

527
00:23:23,835 --> 00:23:26,371
Yes, it feels strange.

528
00:23:26,438 --> 00:23:28,173
All four are drawn differently,

529
00:23:28,240 --> 00:23:29,474
but all are me.

530
00:23:30,041 --> 00:23:31,510
Which one do you like the most?

531
00:23:32,077 --> 00:23:33,545
- The most?
- Yes.

532
00:23:37,149 --> 00:23:38,250
To decide on that,

533
00:23:38,316 --> 00:23:40,719
you need to be very firm about it.

534
00:23:41,553 --> 00:23:42,387
Oh?

535
00:23:42,454 --> 00:23:43,488
NACCHI, HOTARU KUSUNOKI, BAYASHIKO

536
00:23:43,555 --> 00:23:44,556
HOTARU KUSUNOKI

537
00:23:45,390 --> 00:23:46,291
Wait.

538
00:23:46,358 --> 00:23:48,994
Haven’t we seen this person
before somewhere?

539
00:23:50,429 --> 00:23:52,264
That’s me.

540
00:23:54,599 --> 00:23:56,334
It's kind of embarrassing,

541
00:23:56,401 --> 00:23:57,235
but it's a self-portrait.

542
00:23:57,302 --> 00:23:59,104
Impressive! Congratulations!

543
00:23:59,171 --> 00:24:01,206
It looks great!
Can’t put my finger on it though.

544
00:24:01,273 --> 00:24:02,107
You can tell?

545
00:24:02,874 --> 00:24:04,209
Which part do you like?

546
00:24:04,276 --> 00:24:05,710
One second.

547
00:24:05,777 --> 00:24:07,579
Try comparing it.

548
00:24:07,646 --> 00:24:08,814
You’ll see a difference.

549
00:24:12,584 --> 00:24:13,685
This doesn’t have a ring.

550
00:24:13,752 --> 00:24:15,253
- Correct!
- I see!

551
00:24:16,321 --> 00:24:19,391
It somehow feels more natural that way.

552
00:24:20,692 --> 00:24:22,761
I've always wanted to take it off…

553
00:24:23,495 --> 00:24:25,297
Looking at myself, I finally realized it.

554
00:24:26,665 --> 00:24:27,566
I see.

555
00:24:27,632 --> 00:24:28,567
Though…

556
00:24:29,100 --> 00:24:31,670
in reality, things don’t go so smoothly.

557
00:24:32,270 --> 00:24:34,339
Not being able to remove that

558
00:24:34,406 --> 00:24:36,274
is not entirely your fault, Yoshida.

559
00:24:36,975 --> 00:24:39,311
People in the past who hurt you,

560
00:24:39,377 --> 00:24:41,746
the people around you,

561
00:24:42,414 --> 00:24:44,716
and society itself,
I think those are at fault too.

562
00:24:45,484 --> 00:24:47,085
Even so…

563
00:24:47,686 --> 00:24:48,787
That’s why I’m going to…

564
00:24:49,354 --> 00:24:51,389
file a marriage registration form
with Sakuta.

565
00:24:51,456 --> 00:24:52,691
- What?
- What?

566
00:24:52,757 --> 00:24:54,493
We might get hurt,

567
00:24:55,026 --> 00:24:56,528
and it might just end there…

568
00:24:56,595 --> 00:24:58,597
Is that Mr. Hatano's

569
00:24:58,663 --> 00:25:00,532
"love and revolution"?

570
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:02,934
Yes.

571
00:25:04,836 --> 00:25:07,105
It was Sakuta's idea, though.

572
00:25:12,577 --> 00:25:14,312
- Got your hand warmer?
- Yeah.

573
00:25:14,379 --> 00:25:15,947
- What about your exam slip?
- Yeah.

574
00:25:16,014 --> 00:25:17,582
- What about your charm?
- Here.

575
00:25:17,649 --> 00:25:19,584
- Good luck!
- Thanks, I’m off.

576
00:25:27,292 --> 00:25:28,793
Did you pack your water bottle?

577
00:25:42,340 --> 00:25:43,642
Alright, time’s up.

578
00:25:43,708 --> 00:25:46,578
Put your pens down
and turn your papers over.

579
00:25:47,779 --> 00:25:48,713
Nice work.

580
00:25:50,448 --> 00:25:51,716
ENTRANCE EXAMINATION VENUE

581
00:25:51,783 --> 00:25:52,751
Nice work in there.

582
00:25:52,817 --> 00:25:53,885
Thank you.

583
00:25:53,952 --> 00:25:55,020
- Nice work.
- Thank you.

584
00:25:55,086 --> 00:25:56,888
- Thank you so much.
- Nice work.

585
00:25:56,955 --> 00:25:58,757
- Thank you so much.
- Get home safely.

586
00:25:59,257 --> 00:26:00,091
Good work today.

587
00:26:18,677 --> 00:26:20,312
So how’d it go?

588
00:26:21,079 --> 00:26:22,013
As for solar eclipses,

589
00:26:22,080 --> 00:26:23,782
revolution, and rotation, those I knew.

590
00:26:25,050 --> 00:26:26,017
That's it?

591
00:26:26,084 --> 00:26:28,520
In any case, you made it back home safely.

592
00:26:28,587 --> 00:26:29,588
I'm glad about that.

593
00:26:29,654 --> 00:26:31,423
- Good job today.
- Yeah.

594
00:26:33,758 --> 00:26:35,660
- Thank you for the food.
- No problem.

595
00:26:39,030 --> 00:26:40,465
Hatano, that thing.

596
00:26:41,232 --> 00:26:42,367
Right, I almost forgot.

597
00:26:42,434 --> 00:26:43,868
INOKASHIRA APARTMENTS

598
00:26:43,935 --> 00:26:44,936
Good evening.

599
00:26:45,003 --> 00:26:46,605
Oh, good evening.

600
00:26:49,841 --> 00:26:51,076
What's the matter?

601
00:26:51,643 --> 00:26:52,944
I came to see someone.

602
00:26:53,778 --> 00:26:54,646
Who?

603
00:26:55,146 --> 00:26:57,082
Two men…

604
00:26:57,582 --> 00:26:59,217
They’re really…

605
00:26:59,718 --> 00:27:00,785
close, it seems.

606
00:27:03,121 --> 00:27:04,789
They’re in this apartment, yeah.

607
00:27:05,357 --> 00:27:07,459
- Want me to bring you to them?
- No, uh…

608
00:27:09,027 --> 00:27:10,228
They might not be the ones.

609
00:27:11,296 --> 00:27:12,130
What?

610
00:27:12,797 --> 00:27:15,934
Hotaru. Regarding the witnesses
for our marriage registration,

611
00:27:16,001 --> 00:27:18,803
one of them will be my mom…

612
00:27:18,870 --> 00:27:22,040
and I was hoping you could be the other.

613
00:27:24,776 --> 00:27:26,378
"Are you doing well?

614
00:27:26,444 --> 00:27:28,913
Over here, <i>The Sequel:</i>
<i>Three Steps to a Happy Ending</i>

615
00:27:28,980 --> 00:27:30,949
has started,

616
00:27:31,016 --> 00:27:33,418
and I can’t really die
even if I wanted to.

617
00:27:33,485 --> 00:27:36,087
In other words, I’m very well.

618
00:27:36,154 --> 00:27:37,589
Don’t worry.

619
00:27:37,656 --> 00:27:39,958
Well, worry a little, okay?

620
00:27:40,025 --> 00:27:41,993
Anyway, congratulations on your marriage.

621
00:27:42,060 --> 00:27:43,928
By Mom."

622
00:27:43,995 --> 00:27:44,863
Same as always.

623
00:27:44,929 --> 00:27:46,064
Seems like it.

624
00:27:48,266 --> 00:27:49,768
The witness section here.

625
00:27:49,834 --> 00:27:51,436
Can you please fill it out for us?

626
00:27:54,439 --> 00:27:55,306
This form…

627
00:27:55,373 --> 00:27:56,307
MARRIAGE REGISTRATION FORM

628
00:27:56,374 --> 00:27:57,542
Are you really filing it?

629
00:27:58,043 --> 00:28:00,111
HUSBAND-TO-BE: SAKU SAKUTA

630
00:28:11,122 --> 00:28:14,192
HOTARU KUSUNOKI

631
00:28:15,193 --> 00:28:16,895
It's getting late. Want to stay over?

632
00:28:17,762 --> 00:28:18,897
Is that okay?

633
00:28:22,600 --> 00:28:25,203
The people you probably came to see

634
00:28:25,704 --> 00:28:26,938
are in that room over there.

635
00:28:30,942 --> 00:28:32,010
Tomorrow,

636
00:28:32,510 --> 00:28:34,212
if you feel like seeing them, you can.

637
00:28:37,615 --> 00:28:38,783
Sorry about this.

638
00:28:39,784 --> 00:28:42,620
INOKASHIRA APARTMENTS

639
00:28:44,556 --> 00:28:45,423
Yes?

640
00:28:46,825 --> 00:28:48,026
Good morning.

641
00:28:48,093 --> 00:28:49,494
Good morning.

642
00:28:50,495 --> 00:28:52,130
You're from the guitar workshop…

643
00:28:52,630 --> 00:28:53,698
CHASU, CHAN

644
00:28:53,765 --> 00:28:54,632
Um…

645
00:28:57,736 --> 00:28:58,570
This…

646
00:28:59,170 --> 00:29:00,305
hoodie.

647
00:29:01,573 --> 00:29:03,041
Are you two the ones wearing it?

648
00:29:04,609 --> 00:29:06,745
Yeah, that's us.

649
00:29:06,811 --> 00:29:07,812
Yup.

650
00:29:10,115 --> 00:29:11,449
Well, I think…

651
00:29:12,050 --> 00:29:13,051
I might…

652
00:29:17,188 --> 00:29:18,823
be gay too…

653
00:29:21,526 --> 00:29:24,629
We learned in class
that there are people like me,

654
00:29:28,433 --> 00:29:29,768
but around me,

655
00:29:30,535 --> 00:29:32,070
I don’t really see anyone like that.

656
00:29:34,405 --> 00:29:37,075
I haven’t been able
to talk to anyone about it.

657
00:29:46,317 --> 00:29:47,418
There’s someone…

658
00:29:47,919 --> 00:29:49,087
I like.

659
00:29:51,689 --> 00:29:52,524
But

660
00:29:52,590 --> 00:29:55,026
w-when I catch myself

661
00:29:55,093 --> 00:29:57,896
looking at them or thinking about them…

662
00:29:58,463 --> 00:30:01,699
It feels gross, scary, and I dislike it…

663
00:30:02,700 --> 00:30:04,335
The fact that I’m different from others

664
00:30:05,870 --> 00:30:07,038
is something I really hate.

665
00:30:08,807 --> 00:30:11,609
But then, while searching online,

666
00:30:11,676 --> 00:30:12,677
I came across this.

667
00:30:14,746 --> 00:30:15,580
And I realized…

668
00:30:15,647 --> 00:30:18,249
"Ah, I've already met them.

669
00:30:19,717 --> 00:30:21,152
Someone like me

670
00:30:21,653 --> 00:30:23,855
really does exist out there."

671
00:30:26,457 --> 00:30:27,759
When I thought about that…

672
00:30:28,726 --> 00:30:29,861
just a little,

673
00:30:30,461 --> 00:30:32,730
it made me feel better.

674
00:30:34,499 --> 00:30:37,368
I just wanted to say thank you for that.

675
00:30:37,435 --> 00:30:39,237
Really, thank you so much.

676
00:30:40,738 --> 00:30:41,806
I see.

677
00:30:44,309 --> 00:30:45,543
It must be hard on you.

678
00:30:46,778 --> 00:30:47,612
No…

679
00:30:50,281 --> 00:30:51,516
These tears are…

680
00:30:53,017 --> 00:30:55,353
both sad and happy tears.

681
00:30:56,087 --> 00:30:57,388
Half of each.

682
00:30:58,523 --> 00:30:59,557
What does that mean?

683
00:31:01,025 --> 00:31:03,461
I’ve always wanted to talk to someone.

684
00:31:04,896 --> 00:31:06,698
It’s hard,

685
00:31:07,699 --> 00:31:09,634
but I’m happy too now, really.

686
00:31:11,536 --> 00:31:12,871
The person you like…

687
00:31:13,771 --> 00:31:15,073
What do you like about him?

688
00:31:15,773 --> 00:31:17,442
If you don’t mind, tell me.

689
00:31:19,410 --> 00:31:21,246
- What club is he in?
- The basketball club.

690
00:31:23,081 --> 00:31:23,915
Ah…

691
00:31:24,682 --> 00:31:27,819
Does she… know about your relationship?

692
00:31:27,886 --> 00:31:29,721
- You mean Hotaru?
- Yes.

693
00:31:30,355 --> 00:31:31,990
She knows. All too well.

694
00:31:33,157 --> 00:31:34,392
Right.

695
00:31:35,793 --> 00:31:36,861
Don't worry.

696
00:31:37,362 --> 00:31:39,030
We won’t tell her if you don't want it.

697
00:31:40,932 --> 00:31:42,267
Thank you for understanding.

698
00:31:43,201 --> 00:31:44,569
Okay then. See you.

699
00:31:48,206 --> 00:31:50,441
- Take care on your way out.
- Thanks.

700
00:31:55,580 --> 00:31:57,081
- Were you able to see them?
- Yes.

701
00:31:57,682 --> 00:31:58,950
That's good to hear.

702
00:31:59,017 --> 00:32:01,653
Can I visit you again?

703
00:32:01,719 --> 00:32:03,388
Of course!

704
00:32:04,055 --> 00:32:06,591
I’m actually planning to travel soon.

705
00:32:06,658 --> 00:32:09,694
Then please come visit Nagano next time.

706
00:32:09,761 --> 00:32:11,829
Sounds good! I'll definitely go.

707
00:32:13,164 --> 00:32:14,465
Okay then. See you!

708
00:32:14,532 --> 00:32:15,667
See you.

709
00:32:16,367 --> 00:32:19,604
INOKASHIRA APARTMENTS

710
00:32:20,471 --> 00:32:21,873
See you!

711
00:32:24,976 --> 00:32:27,011
Was that a new resident?

712
00:32:27,078 --> 00:32:28,513
Oh, hello.

713
00:32:30,648 --> 00:32:33,384
You really are amazing, Ms. Inokashira.

714
00:32:33,451 --> 00:32:34,752
What, me?

715
00:32:34,819 --> 00:32:36,321
People from all walks of life,

716
00:32:36,387 --> 00:32:39,157
you're able to accept them wholeheartedly.
That's incredible.

717
00:32:39,724 --> 00:32:42,093
That’s my job as a landlady.

718
00:32:44,462 --> 00:32:45,463
Actually, I came today

719
00:32:45,964 --> 00:32:47,598
with a request.

720
00:32:48,933 --> 00:32:50,969
I want to live here.

721
00:32:51,569 --> 00:32:52,403
Really?

722
00:32:52,470 --> 00:32:55,440
I didn’t want to be looked down on.

723
00:32:55,506 --> 00:32:57,375
I wanted people to think I was cool.

724
00:32:57,442 --> 00:32:59,177
That’s why I was looking to buy a condo.

725
00:32:59,243 --> 00:33:01,045
I searched high and low,

726
00:33:01,679 --> 00:33:04,615
but I couldn’t decide on any of them.

727
00:33:05,116 --> 00:33:06,551
Is that so?

728
00:33:07,185 --> 00:33:09,253
Every property I looked at,

729
00:33:09,320 --> 00:33:11,222
I could imagine myself living there.

730
00:33:11,723 --> 00:33:13,424
But every time
I looked at a different one,

731
00:33:13,491 --> 00:33:15,159
I no longer knew which version

732
00:33:15,226 --> 00:33:16,594
of myself I should choose.

733
00:33:18,596 --> 00:33:21,833
Did you imagine yourself living here too?

734
00:33:22,734 --> 00:33:23,735
Yes.

735
00:33:24,602 --> 00:33:25,636
And…

736
00:33:26,471 --> 00:33:29,540
that version of me
felt the most appropriate!

737
00:33:31,109 --> 00:33:32,310
I’ve made up my mind.

738
00:33:32,877 --> 00:33:34,512
My love and revolution…

739
00:33:35,013 --> 00:33:36,414
the person I am now…

740
00:33:36,914 --> 00:33:38,116
it all starts here!

741
00:33:38,616 --> 00:33:40,184
Please accept me.

742
00:33:40,251 --> 00:33:42,286
Of course, I'm more than happy
to welcome you.

743
00:33:42,353 --> 00:33:43,688
Thank you.

744
00:33:44,188 --> 00:33:45,857
Perfect timing, actually.

745
00:33:45,923 --> 00:33:48,226
Mind if I make a request myself too?

746
00:33:48,292 --> 00:33:49,127
What?

747
00:33:50,461 --> 00:33:52,864
The reception is over there, I guess.

748
00:33:52,930 --> 00:33:55,633
CITIZEN AFFAIRS SECTION

749
00:33:58,703 --> 00:34:01,072
Should we just come
another time after all?

750
00:34:01,139 --> 00:34:02,106
But…

751
00:34:02,874 --> 00:34:04,709
it’s not just our problem, right?

752
00:34:05,376 --> 00:34:06,677
Yeah.

753
00:34:08,079 --> 00:34:09,147
Let's go.

754
00:34:13,618 --> 00:34:14,786
Here you go.

755
00:34:14,852 --> 00:34:16,120
MARRIAGE REGISTRATION FORM

756
00:34:19,490 --> 00:34:21,125
Please allow me to check the details.

757
00:34:21,626 --> 00:34:22,593
CITIZEN AFFAIRS SECTION

758
00:34:22,660 --> 00:34:25,063
May I please have your IDs?

759
00:34:25,129 --> 00:34:26,063
Okay.

760
00:34:28,332 --> 00:34:29,767
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

761
00:34:31,135 --> 00:34:32,003
- Here.
- Thank you.

762
00:34:32,970 --> 00:34:33,971
Okay…

763
00:34:34,038 --> 00:34:36,007
GENICHI HATANO, SAKU SAKUTA

764
00:34:36,074 --> 00:34:38,676
Mr. Genichi Hatano…

765
00:34:39,744 --> 00:34:42,013
and Mr. Saku Sakuta.

766
00:34:43,981 --> 00:34:45,283
May I confirm you two…

767
00:34:45,950 --> 00:34:46,851
are male partners?

768
00:34:47,685 --> 00:34:49,087
- Yes.
- That's right.

769
00:34:49,587 --> 00:34:52,490
Please allow me to seek advice.
I will get back to you shortly.

770
00:34:56,327 --> 00:34:57,795
Excuse me.

771
00:34:59,030 --> 00:35:00,064
Can you please…

772
00:35:05,636 --> 00:35:08,306
I’ll need to check with my superior,

773
00:35:08,372 --> 00:35:11,142
so please wait a little longer.
I apologize for the inconvenience.

774
00:35:14,245 --> 00:35:16,013
It’s taking a while, huh?

775
00:35:16,647 --> 00:35:17,849
Yeah.

776
00:35:20,218 --> 00:35:21,853
Sorry to keep you waiting.

777
00:35:22,353 --> 00:35:23,321
This way, please.

778
00:35:23,387 --> 00:35:24,589
Okay.

779
00:35:27,592 --> 00:35:29,293
We’re very sorry,

780
00:35:29,927 --> 00:35:33,131
but we’re unable
to accept this marriage registration.

781
00:35:33,831 --> 00:35:36,534
Considering the both of you
came all the way together,

782
00:35:36,601 --> 00:35:38,269
we truly apologize for that.

783
00:35:39,270 --> 00:35:41,973
No, we should be the ones apologizing

784
00:35:42,039 --> 00:35:43,407
for taking your time.

785
00:35:43,975 --> 00:35:45,209
Thank you for your effort,

786
00:35:45,276 --> 00:35:46,978
- we’re sorry for the trouble.
- Not at all.

787
00:35:47,612 --> 00:35:48,479
But…

788
00:35:48,980 --> 00:35:51,215
the fact that you came today

789
00:35:52,083 --> 00:35:53,117
will be properly

790
00:35:53,751 --> 00:35:54,852
documented.

791
00:35:55,753 --> 00:35:58,556
We’ll ensure it’s reported.

792
00:36:00,024 --> 00:36:01,058
Thank you.

793
00:36:01,626 --> 00:36:02,960
Thank you.

794
00:36:04,462 --> 00:36:05,563
Oh and…

795
00:36:07,732 --> 00:36:10,902
minors cannot act as witnesses.

796
00:36:13,804 --> 00:36:16,073
It was a no-go after all.

797
00:36:16,807 --> 00:36:18,910
We even made a blunder to begin with.

798
00:36:22,180 --> 00:36:25,483
But they said they'll let
their people know about us.

799
00:36:26,384 --> 00:36:27,818
They'll make a report about it.

800
00:36:29,453 --> 00:36:31,756
Our efforts were not wasted, right?

801
00:36:36,294 --> 00:36:37,195
Yup.

802
00:36:39,163 --> 00:36:40,798
It was worth it.

803
00:36:42,500 --> 00:36:43,100
Look, I passed!

804
00:36:43,167 --> 00:36:43,901
PASSED

805
00:36:43,968 --> 00:36:46,103
- Congrats!
- Congrats!

806
00:36:46,170 --> 00:36:47,038
Also…

807
00:36:48,573 --> 00:36:49,607
What is it?

808
00:36:51,576 --> 00:36:52,410
This.

809
00:36:52,476 --> 00:36:53,144
ZENPUKUJI MIDDLE SCHOOL

810
00:36:53,211 --> 00:36:54,812
We got exposed after all,

811
00:36:57,148 --> 00:36:59,617
so it won’t be in the yearbook.

812
00:37:01,652 --> 00:37:03,087
Well, figured.

813
00:37:04,789 --> 00:37:06,224
But,

814
00:37:06,724 --> 00:37:07,858
it was such a great memory!

815
00:37:08,426 --> 00:37:09,460
It was super fun!

816
00:37:09,527 --> 00:37:11,762
I’m going to treasure this.

817
00:37:11,829 --> 00:37:12,997
Me too.

818
00:37:14,699 --> 00:37:15,700
I'll treasure it.

819
00:37:19,804 --> 00:37:21,205
Hotaru!

820
00:37:41,158 --> 00:37:42,927
Are you going on a trip?

821
00:37:42,994 --> 00:37:45,363
Yeah. I realized I could

822
00:37:45,429 --> 00:37:47,698
probably go anywhere,

823
00:37:47,765 --> 00:37:50,568
so I want to see more of the world.

824
00:37:50,635 --> 00:37:51,902
Such as?

825
00:37:51,969 --> 00:37:53,738
For starters, maybe seagulls.

826
00:37:53,804 --> 00:37:55,473
All the different kinds of seagulls.

827
00:37:56,107 --> 00:37:56,941
Sounds good.

828
00:37:57,642 --> 00:37:59,844
Look after things until I get back.

829
00:37:59,910 --> 00:38:01,979
Be nice to my stand-in too, okay?

830
00:38:02,046 --> 00:38:04,181
- Who's that?
- What?

831
00:38:05,116 --> 00:38:06,751
Hey, can you sing for me?

832
00:38:07,318 --> 00:38:09,053
Huh? Sing?

833
00:38:09,120 --> 00:38:11,622
- But I thought you were drawing us?
- Just do it.

834
00:38:12,256 --> 00:38:13,124
Okay.

835
00:38:14,925 --> 00:38:17,595
<i>Today’s place to sleep</i>

836
00:38:17,662 --> 00:38:20,398
<i>Is on a park bench</i>

837
00:38:20,464 --> 00:38:22,900
<i>Sleeping in cramped spots</i>

838
00:38:22,967 --> 00:38:25,436
<i>Is what you're used to</i>

839
00:38:25,503 --> 00:38:26,570
Keep it coming!

840
00:38:27,071 --> 00:38:27,905
Okay.

841
00:38:28,406 --> 00:38:30,775
<i>Tomorrow’s place</i>

842
00:38:30,841 --> 00:38:33,477
<i>Will be in a car</i>

843
00:38:33,544 --> 00:38:35,880
<i>Fallen leaves</i>

844
00:38:35,946 --> 00:38:39,884
<i>Will wrap you up</i>

845
00:38:39,950 --> 00:38:40,951
Louder!

846
00:38:41,519 --> 00:38:44,355
<i>No home, oh, n--</i>

847
00:38:44,422 --> 00:38:47,191
- This has always bugged me, you know?
- What is it?

848
00:38:47,258 --> 00:38:48,759
You do have a home, no?

849
00:38:49,360 --> 00:38:50,428
Right here!

850
00:38:51,195 --> 00:38:52,263
You're right.

851
00:38:52,330 --> 00:38:53,698
She's got a point.

852
00:38:54,198 --> 00:38:55,766
So change it.

853
00:38:56,967 --> 00:38:58,269
Ready, go!

854
00:38:58,336 --> 00:39:00,871
<i>Home</i>

855
00:39:00,938 --> 00:39:03,307
<i>Oh, your sweet home</i>

856
00:39:03,374 --> 00:39:06,077
All of Japan, no, the whole world
is all ears!

857
00:39:07,611 --> 00:39:10,214
<i>Home</i>

858
00:39:10,281 --> 00:39:12,516
<i>Oh, your sweet home</i>

859
00:39:12,583 --> 00:39:15,486
<i>The vast sky</i>

860
00:39:15,553 --> 00:39:17,321
<i>Is your roof</i>

861
00:39:17,388 --> 00:39:18,222
More!

862
00:39:18,289 --> 00:39:20,358
<i>The day after tomorrow…</i>

863
00:39:20,424 --> 00:39:23,060
<i>The day after tomorrow…</i>

864
00:39:23,127 --> 00:39:26,097
<i>Let's go look for</i>

865
00:39:26,163 --> 00:39:28,699
<i>Your new home</i>

866
00:39:28,766 --> 00:39:30,601
<i>After the beep tone,</i>

867
00:39:30,668 --> 00:39:33,537
<i>please leave your name and message.</i>

868
00:39:34,038 --> 00:39:35,873
<i>Hello, Mr. Hatano?</i>

869
00:39:35,940 --> 00:39:37,641
<i>Things got hectic after that</i>

870
00:39:37,708 --> 00:39:39,744
<i>and we never really got to talk,</i>

871
00:39:39,810 --> 00:39:41,078
<i>so I thought I’d call.</i>

872
00:39:41,746 --> 00:39:43,681
<i>I’m doing my best over here.</i>

873
00:39:44,248 --> 00:39:46,083
<i>- I haven't skipped school either.</i>
- Ah, Hotaru!

874
00:39:46,717 --> 00:39:49,320
<i>Also, my mom calls me every day.</i>

875
00:39:49,387 --> 00:39:50,221
<i>It's a bit annoying.</i>

876
00:39:51,989 --> 00:39:55,126
<i>Her company forgave what she did,</i>

877
00:39:55,192 --> 00:39:57,728
<i>which allowed her</i>
<i>to be released from the police.</i>

878
00:39:59,029 --> 00:40:00,564
<i>- You know…</i>
- Hey, Koharu!

879
00:40:00,631 --> 00:40:01,499
Let me see.

880
00:40:01,565 --> 00:40:03,534
<i>…until my mom left home,</i>

881
00:40:04,168 --> 00:40:06,604
- Be careful, okay?
<i>- I thought places like Toyoko…</i>

882
00:40:07,104 --> 00:40:07,972
There.

883
00:40:09,740 --> 00:40:10,674
How does it look?

884
00:40:13,611 --> 00:40:15,846
Looks… good!

885
00:40:15,913 --> 00:40:17,148
Good boy.

886
00:40:17,214 --> 00:40:19,150
<i>…or my divorced dad…</i>

887
00:40:19,216 --> 00:40:20,851
Good boy.

888
00:40:20,918 --> 00:40:22,820
<i>or gay people…</i>

889
00:40:22,887 --> 00:40:24,221
I've decided on this place.

890
00:40:24,722 --> 00:40:26,223
Very well.

891
00:40:26,290 --> 00:40:29,059
- Alright, please fill out this form…
- Mr. Okabe.

892
00:40:30,361 --> 00:40:33,764
Could you watch me while I take this off?

893
00:40:33,831 --> 00:40:34,698
Sure.

894
00:40:35,766 --> 00:40:38,269
I’m going to start afresh from here!

895
00:40:48,913 --> 00:40:49,980
Welcome!

896
00:40:50,481 --> 00:40:51,782
This is for me,

897
00:40:51,849 --> 00:40:53,484
the landlady's stand-in,

898
00:40:53,551 --> 00:40:56,086
and Mrs. Tomoe. I got <i>dango</i> for us.

899
00:40:56,153 --> 00:40:56,987
Really?

900
00:40:57,521 --> 00:40:59,156
Mrs. Tomoe!

901
00:40:59,223 --> 00:41:02,193
- We've got some <i>dango!</i>
- Coming!

902
00:41:02,259 --> 00:41:04,495
<i>…or those news-type incidents…</i>

903
00:41:09,066 --> 00:41:10,501
<i>or even animals…</i>

904
00:41:12,303 --> 00:41:15,606
<i>I thought none of it had</i>
<i>anything to do with me.</i>

905
00:41:16,106 --> 00:41:17,975
- Be careful not to collapse them.
- Okay.

906
00:41:18,042 --> 00:41:20,010
<i>But I was wrong.</i>

907
00:41:21,645 --> 00:41:22,847
<i>Everything in this world</i>

908
00:41:22,913 --> 00:41:25,483
<i>might be connected to me</i>
<i>in some way, I thought.</i>

909
00:41:28,052 --> 00:41:29,520
<i>And if I keep thinking that way,</i>

910
00:41:30,087 --> 00:41:32,323
<i>maybe I can become a kinder person.</i>

911
00:41:37,862 --> 00:41:41,098
<i>There was something I meant</i>
<i>to give you and Mr. Sakuta.</i>

912
00:41:41,932 --> 00:41:43,634
<i>Has it arrived yet?</i>

913
00:41:44,435 --> 00:41:47,905
<i>I just kept eating them</i>
<i>until I finally got a winning stick.</i>

914
00:41:49,173 --> 00:41:51,775
<i>It’s my own way of saying thank you</i>
<i>for everything.</i>

915
00:41:53,043 --> 00:41:55,246
<i>Really… thank you for all you did.</i>

916
00:41:55,746 --> 00:41:57,781
<i>Okay then. Talk to you again.</i>

917
00:41:58,382 --> 00:41:59,683
Ah, there you are.

918
00:42:01,385 --> 00:42:03,687
This spot is nice, isn't it?

919
00:42:04,221 --> 00:42:05,055
Yes.

920
00:42:08,325 --> 00:42:10,160
You carry that around with you?

921
00:42:10,961 --> 00:42:13,564
Yes, as a charm. How about you, Sakuta?

922
00:42:14,598 --> 00:42:16,000
I’m afraid of losing it…

923
00:42:18,636 --> 00:42:19,803
so it's always in here.

924
00:42:20,304 --> 00:42:22,072
- I knew it.
- There you have it.

925
00:42:25,509 --> 00:42:26,644
Sakuta.

926
00:42:27,578 --> 00:42:28,812
What is it?

927
00:42:28,879 --> 00:42:31,248
Until we can actually file
the marriage registration…

928
00:42:32,149 --> 00:42:33,017
Let’s stay together.

929
00:42:33,083 --> 00:42:34,718
What’s that all of a sudden?

930
00:42:35,286 --> 00:42:37,955
Let’s be together forever
until we can buy a house.

931
00:42:40,658 --> 00:42:43,227
- Okay.
- Forever, and I mean it.

932
00:42:43,727 --> 00:42:44,562
Let's stay together.

933
00:42:45,496 --> 00:42:46,530
Yeah, okay.

934
00:42:47,031 --> 00:42:48,699
U-Um!

935
00:42:48,766 --> 00:42:51,001
Sorry to bother you while you’re busy…

936
00:42:52,136 --> 00:42:54,471
- Hm?
- The next pair for the viewing are here.

937
00:42:55,172 --> 00:42:56,240
Let's go.

938
00:42:56,307 --> 00:42:57,207
This way.

939
00:42:58,075 --> 00:42:59,677
Come on.

940
00:43:03,414 --> 00:43:05,983
WINNER

941
00:44:53,390 --> 00:44:55,893
Subtitle translation by: Jeffery
